\f0\fs24 \cf0 NovaUI \'97 Project Overview (Phase 2)\
===================================\
\
Goal\
----\
NovaUI is the React frontend for Nova\'92s microservice platform (user, product, order services). Phase 2 adds preview authentication so operators can explore protected workflows before the dedicated auth service arrives in Phase 3.\
\
Core Stack\
----------\
- React 19 + TypeScript (Vite)\
- Tailwind CSS for styling\
- Zustand for application and auth state\
- Axios with auth-aware interceptors\
- Recharts for dashboard analytics\
- Docker & docker-compose for environment parity\
\
Environments\
------------\
The repo mirrors backend environments (dev, test, preprod, prod). Each folder contains a compose file and `.env` with service URLs plus auth settings.\
\
.env settings\
- `VITE_ENV` \'97 environment label displayed in the UI header\
- `VITE_USER_API`, `VITE_PRODUCT_API`, `VITE_ORDER_API` \'97 service endpoints per environment\
- `VITE_AUTH_API` \'97 placeholder auth endpoint used by the mock API\
- `VITE_AUTH_TOKEN_KEY` \'97 storage key for JWT-like tokens (currently `nova_token`)\
\
Mock Authentication (Phase 2)\
-----------------------------\
- `authApi.ts` simulates login/logout with demo users (Admin, Staff, Courier). Successful logins receive a locally minted JWT-style token.\
- `authStore.ts` (Zustand) persists the session, stores the token in `localStorage`, restores on refresh, and exposes helpers like `hasRole`.\
- `authHelpers` encode/decode mock tokens; JWT validation hooks are ready for future backend integration.\
- Axios requests automatically attach the bearer token when present.\
\
UI & Routing Changes\
--------------------\
- `/login` \'97 new sign-in screen using `AuthForm` with quick-fill demo accounts.\
- `/unauthorized` \'97 friendly page for blocked access attempts.\
- `/profile` \'97 shows current user identity, email, role, and storage strategy.\
- `ProtectedRoute` guard wraps the app shell and individual routes for role checks.\
- Role-based navigation filters sidebar/mobile links and disables create actions for couriers.\
- Navbar and mobile drawer display the active user, role badge, environment chip, and logout control.\
\
Role Access Matrix\
------------------\
- Admin: full access (dashboard, users, products, orders, payment, profile)\
- Staff: dashboard, products, orders, payment, profile\
- Courier: orders (read-only) and profile\
\
Operations Console Enhancements\
--------------------------------\
- Orders page adapts based on role: couriers can monitor status while admin/staff retain full creation and status-change capabilities.\
- Logout clears auth state and Nova data cache to prepare for the next login.\
- Dashboard now surfaces API health banners and supports auth-aware refresh flows.\
\
Existing Data Workflows\
-----------------------\
- Users: CRUD (list, create, delete with validation feedback)\
- Products: create/update/delete with inventory analytics\
- Orders: create, update status, real-time analytics and recent activity\
- Payment: simulation card for future Kafka integration\
- Toast notifications unify success/error feedback across flows\
\
Docker & Scripts\
----------------\
- `Dockerfile.dev` and `npm run docker:dev` power local hot reload.\
- Production image builds via `npm run build` in a two-stage Dockerfile (Node -> Nginx).\
- Each environment compose file sets unique container/image names (`novaui-<env>`) and standard ports (dev 5173, test 3001, preprod 3002, prod 3000).\
\
Future Work (Phase 3+)\
----------------------\
- Swap mock auth API with real `auth-service` endpoints and refresh token cycle.\
- Introduce session expiry notices, multi-factor auth, and Kafka-driven global logout.\
- Expand audit views (event timeline, DLQ monitoring) as backend events mature.\
\
Summary\
-------\
NovaUI now enforces mock authentication, role-based navigation, and secure route guards while retaining the operational dashboards built in Phase 1. The frontend is ready to integrate the real authentication microservice planned for Phase 3.\
